  "product": "GTS",
  "name": "Talking Chatter",
  "author": "Riddim Rack",
  "description": "A mouth that says four different syllables every half bar: a stepped LFO locked to the 1/2 grid jumps a Formant filter through four vowel positions, one per eighth note, with a slight glide between them, like a vocoded robot reading out loud. A Reed layer and a Vowel-table layer feed the filter, tube drive adds bite, and a clean sine sub at the played pitch keeps the low end steady and mono. Play: held F1 to A#1 notes at 140 to 150 BPM, or short riffs, and let it chatter over the kick. Macros: Syllables widens how far the vowels jump and opens the top end so the consonants cut, Mouth sharpens the vowel peaks so they ring, Glide smears the steps into each other for a smoother, rounder talk, Chatter adds a fast sixteenth-note flutter on the Reed layer with a little extra bite.",
  "category": "Bass/formant",
  "tags": [
    "formant",
    "talking",
    "call-response",
    "mono"
  ],
